  "query_preview": "..\nToday through Monday: A dry air mass will remain over the Inland\nNW through Sunday night with precipitable water values ranging \nfrom near 40-70 percent of normal. This combined with light \nwinds will promote strong radiational cooling with areas of \nfrost. A Frost Advisory remains in effect through 9 AM this \nmorning for areas still within their climatological growing \nseason where areas of frost are forecast. For the northern \nmountain valleys and ID Panhandle the average first frost occurs\naround September 15th-25th and thus the reason for no \nadvisories since frost is more common this time of year, \nalthough many areas still have not received their first frost \nyet, with another cool night in store for Sunday Night. For high\ntemperatures gradual warming is expected for Sunday and Monday \nas southwest flow develops ahead of the next system. High \ntemperatures on Monday will be right near normal values with \nreadings in the mid 60s to low 70s.\n\nMonday Night and Tuesday: A weak atmospheric river takes aim at\nthe region with an increase in moisture as precipitable water\nincreases to 150-200 percent of normal. Yet with the strong\nwesterly flow and dry air mass to start, precipitation will have a\nhard time reaching the ground other than potential sprinkles, and\na chance for light rain over the northern mountains. Upslope flow\ninto the Cascade crest will lead to wet conditions with around\n0.50-1.00 inch of rain, with light rain spilling over the crest\ninto the upper reaches of the Methow Valley, Lake Chelan, and Lake\nWenatchee.\n\nWednesday through Saturday: Following Tuesday's influx of clouds\nand areas of light rain or sprinkles, the weather looks very \nquiet for the rest of the week. A mild west-southwest flow \npattern occurs for the rest of the week with weak ridging bringing\nnear to slightly above normal temperatures. About 25 percent of\nthe model clusters show the stronger ridge building in sooner, by\nFriday, which would result in a more rapid warming trend by\nSaturday if realized. JW",
